1.1 This standard specifies the requirements of elastomer/rubber/silicon insulated cables for fixed wiring cables, flexible cables and flexible cords for electric power and lighting for operation at voltages up to and including 1 100 volts.
1.2 The following types of cables and cords are covered in this standard:
1.2.1 Cables for Fixed Wiring
a) Braided and compounded/varnished;
b) Elastomer sheathed (normal duty);
c) Elastomer sheathed (normal duty) with earth continuity conductor;
d) Rubber insulated and/or sheathed cables; and
e) Silicon Insulated and/or sheathed cables.
1.2.2 Flexible Cables
a) Braided and varnished;
b) Elastomer sheathed (heavy duty); and
c) Rubber/silicon insulated sheathed cables.
1.2.3 Flexible Cords
a) Braided or unbraided;
b) Elastomer Sheathed (normal duty);
c) Unkinkable flexible cords - braided and compounded (workshop type); and
d) Unkinkable flexible cords - braided and compounded.
